{"schema_version":3,"catalogue_version":1,"id":"bco:33-4","provision":"BCO 33-4","book":"bco","book_name":"Book of Church Order","abbreviation":"BCO","reference":"33-4","title":"Section 33-4","supplementary":false,"canonical_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/provisions/bco/33-4/","reader_url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-constitution-reader/#bco/33-4","current_text":{"html":"<p>When it is impracticable immediately to commence process against an accused church member, the Session may, if it thinks the edification of the Church requires it, prevent the accused from approaching the Lord's Table until the charges against him can be examined, but this requires a two-thirds (2/3) majority.</p>","text":"When it is impracticable immediately to commence process against an accused church member, the Session may, if it thinks the edification of the Church requires it, prevent the accused from approaching the Lord's Table until the charges against him can be examined, but this requires a two-thirds (2/3) majority."},"source":{"name":"PCA Constitution Reader","revision":"3215b08b64db0d1ab36e0721b999ec192d812d74","edition":"Current Reader text","files":{"bco.js":"c88e552545b73fd9690de620b237895b7ea52a94bed8e95690c116bf76be8ae5","wcf.js":"1ebf9e54223f7fe4e728a3e640c833a435af825d74b5ef3d4b04687685538a0d","wlc.js":"f6977e761ea4ccc93b07fcacfd0391890cb05b42f4317d807fa293c078d9b051","wsc.js":"dd775417f7ef21e3283bacad5e6ef193c41d64d03bd5a2e8fb934ccca8cb8e53","rao.js":"49808bbb0e95abdc3b07506c87dde0d62d087851e869b49c0f1f2424986450ec"}},"input_fingerprint":"e5fd669690c4b80754c46f09d04273adf2ccbfb6563342677c52c5cde8a91808","assessment_fingerprint":"517b100d2e9006e313ab6d84d4f0f31593b77832f395383ba2227779470cd034","assessment_summary":{"status":"stale","file":"index/provision_link_adjudications.jsonl","total":11481,"expected":12455,"applied":0,"stale":11481,"unmatched":0,"unassessed":12455},"parent_id":"bco:33","children":[],"coverage":{"relationships":"indexed_records"