.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:33-4--case:cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.md:occ-e1ad190b37c1","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":36},"excerpt":"…until the charges against her were adjudicated and removed. Session cited BCO 33-4. The charges were not revealed in the citation letter. This citation was made approximately one year after the congregational meeting that considered dissolving the…","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.md"},{"id":"bco:33-4--case:cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.md:occ-806afa9ae0f2","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":288},"excerpt":"In the Session's letter to Mrs. Smith that cited her to appear and hear charges, the Session cited BCO 33-4 and placed her under suspension from the sacraments until the charges against her were \"adjudicated and removed.\" (ROC 70) However, the charges","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.md"},{"id":"bco:33-4--case:cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.md:occ-b4cb2a94033c","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":294},"excerpt":"BCO 33-4 states:","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.md"},{"id":"bco:33-4--case:cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.md:occ-b9f0e5ef75f3","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.html","repository_path":"cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":298},"excerpt":"However, the conditions required by BCO 33-4 were not met. There is no indication that it was \"impracticable immediately to commence process\" against Mrs. Smith. In fact, process was commenced within a reasonable time.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga28_2000__1998-08.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"topics":["appeal","discipline","evidence","witnesses","burden of proof","presumption of guilt","contumacy","suspension from sacraments","procedural errors","factiousness","slander","divisiveness","membership vows","case in process","panel"],"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1998-8"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Smith appealed discipline for divisiveness, gossip and slander, broken membership vows, and contumacy arising largely from complaints and letters during church conflict. The SJC sustained her appeal, reversed guilt on all four charges, and annulled suspension from the sacraments. The documentary record proved none of the allegations; filing complaints was not itself divisiveness, and the trial improperly lacked a witness, shifted proof to Smith, showed prejudice, and unfairly rejected her written defense. The SJC declined remand because the evidence was insufficient."}},{"id":"bco:33-4--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-09.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-09.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"William A. Conrad et al. v. Central Carolina Presbytery","year":1994,"disposition":"out_of_order","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-09.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-09.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:33-4--case:cases/ga22_1994__1993-09.md:occ-6e47ecbba993","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga22_1994__1993-09.html","repository_path":"cases/ga22_1994__1993-09.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":48},"excerpt":"…suspension to the men in question. In doing this action the Commission cited BCO 33-4 as the authority for carrying out this action. Again only one Ruling Elder was present, and therefore a quorum was not present.","sources":["case_markdown_text","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_as","cases.jsonl:bco_cited_current","judicial_cases.jsonl:bco_provisions"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga22_1994__1993-09.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"standard_of_review":"not_stated","case_numbers":["1993-9"],"body":"SJC"}},{"id":"bco:33-4--case:cases/ga23_1995__1994-04.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga23_1995__1994-04.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"William A. Conrad et al. vs. Central Carolina Presbytery","year":null,"disposition":"","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga23_1995__1994-04.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga23_1995__1994-04.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:33-4--case:cases/ga23_1995__1994-04.md:occ-509c328c0407","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga23_1995__1994-04.html","repository_path":"cases/ga23_1995__1994-04.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":44},"excerpt":"…suspension to the men in question. In doing this action th